    {
      "category": "overview",
      "field": "description",
      "value": "Despite dancing around spirituality, leading many to consider Confucianism as a philosophy only, the religion establishes a theological understanding of the Universe, albeit an impersonal one. In it, the priority of humankind is to strive to synchronize with the order of the universe in order to achieve oneness with heaven for the tranquility of community and self. This order is defined by 'Tiān,' a non-speaking 'God of Heaven' which can be best translated as 'the way things are.'",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "source": null,
      "metadata": {
        "chunk_id": "page_0011",
        "chunk_title": "9. Confucianism",
        "chunk_order": 10,
        "source_type": "page"
      }
    },
